# Fundamental Python Programming Assignments
### Course Portfolio Overview (B.Tech Computer Science & Engineering)

This repository contains a comprehensive collection of 45 structural Python scripts designed to establish proficiency across fundamental computer science principles, variable management, manual control flow structures, and core data tracking algorithms.

---

## 🛠️ Repository Architecture & Milestones

The assignment library is organized into progressive, modular problem sets that document a continuous development pipeline over the semester:

### Module 1: Core Python Syntaxes & Operations (August 22)
*   **`solution1.py`** - Console output management: Render formatted string lines to standard outputs.
*   **`solution2.py`** - Primitive variable structures: Declare, store, and compute the sum of distinct integers.
*   **`solution3.py`** - Binary conditional boundaries: Evaluate age milestones using standard if-else validation gates.
*   **`solution4.py`** - Linear tracking collections: Access and print items sequentially out of standard array lists.
*   **`solution5.py`** - Basic index iterators: Construct sequential incremental counter parameters running from 1 up to 5.

### Module 2: Control Flow Abstractions (August 27)
*   **`solution6.py`** - Arithmetic expression compilation: Execute addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division operations on double data entries.
*   **`solution7.py`** - String concatenation metrics: Combine distinct data string inputs into unified personalized messages.
*   **`solution8.py`** - Modulo logic applications: Evaluate integer values via modulo arithmetic blocks (`%`) to categorize numbers as odd or even.
*   **`solution9.py`** - Array sequence traversal: Parse raw collections of string arrays dynamically using structured index loops.
*   **`solution10.py`** - Manual loop constraints: Configure iterative loops using structural increment handlers to execute exactly 3 cycles.

### Module 3: Manual Algorithmic Control Structures (September 2)
*   **`solution11.py`** - String slice indexing: Implement manual array index traversal to detect structural palindrome sequences.
*   **`solution12.py`** - Academic grade filtering: Traverse raw numeric score records to track data quantities passing specific thresholds.
*   **`solution13.py`** - Manual peak detection: Track down the maximum value out of numeric arrays directly via linear comparisons without native abstraction wrappers.
*   **`solution14.py`** - Dictionary lookup calculators: Model transactional store checkouts using map entries to track pricing variables and compile billing parameters.
*   **`solution15.py`** - Lower-level linear scanners: Build search paths using boolean flag indicators to verify the structural existence of query elements in a list.

